group_id":null,"id":"f42c9c64b7ba06ebd","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"/health auth exemption section + AC line 1 (in-process ASGI /health) and AC auth-exemption oracle","norm_id":"nfcd7e3e177a7b2c6","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["custom_route does not exist (or has a different name/signature) in mcp 1.28.x → build_server wiring fails and the /health endpoint never mounts","custom_route mounts INSIDE the auth middleware scope → an unauthenticated HEALTHCHECK/probe of /health returns 401, failing the auth-exemption AC and breaking the container HEALTHCHECK + foxterrier retire check under REBAR_MCP_AUTH_ENABLED=1"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"insufficient","asserted_capability_confirmed":"insufficient","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"insufficient","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify `logging: driver: journald` on the new `mcp` compose service, matching the existing gerrit/review-bot/opcert services and the S2 observability AC.","cohort":["T10"],"criteria":["T10"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.35,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["docker-compose.yml: gerrit/review-bot/opcert each declare `logging: driver: journald`","Plan Scope lists restart/healthcheck/stop_grace_period/env for the mcp service but does not mention a logging driver"],"finding":"The plan does not state that the new `mcp` compose service uses `logging: driver: journald`. Every existing service in docker-compose.yml (gerrit, review-bot, opcert) sets journald per the S2 observability AC so container logs land in the host journal; without it the new service would default to the json-file driver and be inconsistent with the box's observability model.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb6504b6c792c275f","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope — docker-compose.yml `mcp` service","norm_id":"n9e9f8a66f4d8852c","priority":0.55,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Operator runs `journalctl CONTAINER_NAME=compose-mcp-1` and finds no logs because the service defaults to json-file"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Add `logging: driver: journald` to the `mcp` service block in docker-compose.yml.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"incomplete_enumeration","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify atomic/lock-guarded mutation of the `in_flight` gauge and a race-free SIGTERM drain check (no TOCTOU between the zero-read and a concurrent increment), and add a concurrent-inflight test to the AC.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T12","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.engine-layer-enforcement","project.portability"],"criteria":["T9"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"an integer `in_flight` gauge counting ONLY certified ops\"","\"On SIGTERM the process waits up to 1200s for `in_flight` to reach 0, then exits\"","ABSENCE: no statement that gauge increment/decrement or the drain-check is atomic/lock-guarded under concurrent async requests"],"finding":"The `in_flight` gauge is mutable state incremented/decremented by concurrently-running certified ops under an async ASGI server, but the plan never specifies that mutation is atomic (lock/atomic counter) nor that the SIGTERM drain (\"waits up to 1200s for `in_flight` to reach 0\") is free of a check-then-act race against concurrent inc/dec.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f27cae3d1e39d970a","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"/health gauge section + SIGTERM grace section (`src/rebar/_mcp_health.py`)","norm_id":"nf18043f412f7d615","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Two certified ops start/finish concurrently and a non-atomic ++/-- loses an update, so `in_flight` never reflects true count.","SIGTERM fires, drain loop reads in_flight==0 between a decrement and a new increment (TOCTOU), and the process exits mid-op — the exact outcome the grace was meant to prevent."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"State that the gauge uses a threading/asyncio lock or an atomic counter for inc/dec and that the SIGTERM drain re-checks under the same lock; add an AC exercising two overlapping certified ops.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.1429,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"low","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reconcile the SIGTERM-grace mechanism with uvicorn: implement the in-flight drain as an ASGI lifespan shutdown hook (the review_bot app.py/reconcile.py precedent) that uvicorn awaits, rather than a raw signal.signal(SIGTERM) handler that races uvicorn's own handler — and drive the test through the same run() path.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.5069,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["mcp_server.py:736 `server.run(transport=\"streamable-http\" ...)` — FastMCP streamable-http runs under uvicorn, which installs its own SIGTERM handler","review_bot precedent drains in-flight work via an ASGI lifespan shutdown hook: review_bot/app.py:113 `async def lifespan`, reconcile.py:310 'the lifespan waits for the review in flight', config.py:33-50 DEFAULT_SHUTDOWN_DRAIN_SECONDS bounded by queue.join()","Plan: '_mcp_health.py ... On SIGTERM the process waits up to 1200s ...' + Testing: 'a subprocess/signal SIGTERM test' — describes a raw signal handler, not a lifespan hook"],"finding":"The SIGTERM grace is specified as a raw signal handler in _mcp_health.py, but the server runs under uvicorn (main() -> server.run(transport='streamable-http')), whose own SIGTERM handler drives shutdown by awaiting the ASGI lifespan shutdown phase — the exact seam the in-repo review_bot precedent uses to drain in-flight work. A hand-installed signal handler races/is preempted by uvicorn's, so the gauge-drain may not run as designed.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fe406b4ca265cefe8","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"SIGTERM grace (concrete numbers); AC-4; Scope bullet '_mcp_health.py'","norm_id":"n729923e6e71e1425","priority":0.2931,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Container receives SIGTERM while a certified op is in flight; uvicorn's handler fires and begins its own shutdown, so the _mcp_health signal handler's drain either never runs or double-drives shutdown"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Mirror review_bot: register a lifespan whose shutdown phase waits (bounded by DEFAULT_SHUTDOWN_GRACE_SECONDS) for the in_flight gauge to reach 0, wired into the FastMCP streamable_http_app, and assert the drain through that lifespan rather than a standalone signal handler.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.4375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"insufficient","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"insufficient","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"insufficient"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reconcile DEFAULT_SHUTDOWN_GRACE_SECONDS with ADR 0104 §2's rejection of a gauge-gated drain bound: state explicitly that this 1200s wait is a Docker-SIGKILL BACKSTOP (foxterrier's retire-when-idle keeps it unreachable in normal operation) whose worst-case kill is safe because event-sourced writes are idempotently re-requested (ADR lines 85-87) — or drop the hard bounded exit if it is not actually needed.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["ADR 0104 lines 78-81: 'a shared MCP server driven by N agents ... an in_flight gauge may never reach 0; a gauge-gated drain bound would then be exhausted and KILL an in-flight certified op, and merely enlarging the bound only defers the same kill'","ADR 0104 lines 81-82: blue-green 'decouples retirement from the deploy, so a never-idle server never blocks a deploy and never forces a kill'","Plan: 'On SIGTERM the process waits up to 1200s for in_flight to reach 0, then exits' — a bounded gauge-gated drain whose exhaustion kills an in-flight op, exactly the mechanism the ADR rejects","Plan states the gauge 'does not gate the deploy' and 'retirement waits on billable work', but never explains why a hard 1200s exit here does not resurrect the ADR's rejected kill-on-exhaustion"],"finding":"The plan's bounded SIGTERM grace (DEFAULT_SHUTDOWN_GRACE_SECONDS=1200, 'then exits') reintroduces the gauge-gated drain BOUND that the governing ADR explicitly rejected as unsafe for a shared MCP server, and the plan does not reconcile this contradiction.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f65f3c1935b17cbce","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"SIGTERM grace (concrete numbers); Approach; Compat/rollback","norm_id":"n7f09e0a909e79e78","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Docker issues SIGTERM (e.g. host reboot, OOM, manual stop, or a foxterrier retire that fires before the op finishes) while a minutes-to-longer certified op exceeds 1200s -> the bound exhausts and the in-flight certified op is killed — the precise outcome ADR 0104 §2 designed blue-green to avoid"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2857,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"na","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State how `REBAR_MCP_AUTH_STATIC_TOKENS_FILE` is materialized on the box (which slice/script writes it from SSM, at 0600, before `docker compose up`, and how the bind-mount source is guaranteed present) — or explicitly cite avians as owning that step and note the fail-closed behavior when the file is absent.","cohort":["T10"],"criteria":["T10"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8175,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: `REBAR_MCP_AUTH_STATIC_TOKENS_FILE` listed as compose env, `REBAR_MCP_AUTH_ENABLED=1`, `REBAR_MCP_AUTH_STRATEGIES=static`","search_files infra/ for REBAR_MCP_AUTH_STATIC_TOKENS_FILE → (no matches): no on-box materialization exists today","Precedent: opcert/g2p/deploy-key secrets are materialized from SSM to 0600 files BEFORE `docker compose up` (materialize-opcert-guard.sh, fetch-secrets.sh); the plan defers to avians but does not name the on-box seam or how the bind-mount source is guaranteed present"],"finding":"The compose `mcp` service sets REBAR_MCP_AUTH_STATIC_TOKENS_FILE (the file the static-bearer verifier reads to authenticate every /mcp caller), but the plan does not specify how that tokens file is materialized on the box before boot. A repo search finds no existing materialization path, and the fail-closed auth posture (and thus the internet-reachable /mcp endpoint's human/agent-auth contract) depends on that file existing.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd65cf1fbb8c0558f","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope — docker-compose.yml env list; Compat/rollback (\"secrets in avians\")","norm_id":"n80f297d08e11e9a0","priority":0.0825,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Fresh boot with no tokens file present: the static verifier has no accepted tokens (or the bind-mount source is missing and docker creates a directory), so /mcp auth is broken or the container fails to start","The foxterrier/avians slice boundary leaves nobody clearly owning the token-file materialization step in compose-up.sh"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Add a note that the tokens file is materialized by the avians slice (fetch-secrets.sh / a materialize-mcp-tokens.sh mirroring the opcert precedent) into a 0600 file bind-mounted read-only, and describe the /mcp behavior when the file is absent (fail-closed 401).","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes",